;; Configuration for the documentation site, read by the jlt-commons
;; docs-engine (https://github.com/jlt-commons/docs-engine).
;;
;; Build it locally from a docs-engine checkout with `bb build <this repo>`,
;; or `bb serve <this repo>` to preview.
;;
;; NOTHING PUBLISHES IT at the moment. The workflow that did was removed while
;; this repository is private: GitHub Pages is unavailable for a private
;; repository on this plan, so its deploy step failed on every push. This file
;; and everything it configures are kept ready for the day it is restored,
;; which is one call to jlt-commons/ci-builds/.github/workflows/site.yml@main.
{;; :base-path is what makes this a project site rather than an org one. The
 ;; site is served at https://jlt-commons.github.io/raylib-android/, so every URL
 ;; the engine emits needs that prefix. Leave it out and the pages still
 ;; render, but each one loads the ORGANIZATION site's stylesheet and every
 ;; image 404s.
 :base-path   "/raylib-android"

 :title       "raylib-android"
 :description "raylib on an Android phone, driven from Clojure on Chez Scheme via Jolt. Seventeen scenes as native arm64 code in a NativeActivity, with no JVM, no Kotlin and no Java in the app."

 ;; docs/images holds the GIFs and stills, referenced from the homepage and
 ;; the guides. Without this the pages render with every image broken, and the
 ;; engine only warns about a missing asset dir, so docs/check-site.sh turns
 ;; that into an error.
 :asset-dirs  ["images"]

 ;; Relative to docs/templates/. Drop this line and the engine renders a
 ;; generic homepage from docs/guide/index.md instead.
 :home-template "home.html"}
